From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:19:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: gs101: describe the PMU's address space

The google,gs101-pmu binding now describes the power domains as children
of the PMU, addressed by their offset in it, and requires the address
and size cells and ranges on the PMU node. Add them, with the PMU's
64 KiB mapped from offset 0. No child uses them yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101.dtsi | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101.dtsi
index 4ac27abd5..e9f3c1adc 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101.dtsi
@@ -1804,6 +1804,9 @@ sysreg_apm: syscon@17420000 {
 		pmu_system_controller: system-controller@17460000 {
 			compatible = "google,gs101-pmu";
 			reg = <0x17460000 0x10000>;
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <1>;
+			ranges = <0x0 0x17460000 0x10000>;
 			google,pmu-intr-gen-syscon = <&pmu_intr_gen>;
 
 			poweroff: syscon-poweroff {
